## Summary

I found the previous (uncommitted) work already in the tree — analytics instrumentation for VISION.md's TODO item ("Instrument the target metric..."). It had a real bug: `TodayViewModel` referenced an undeclared `lastPublishedUnlockedBuddyCount` while a differently-named property (`mutualRevealFiredForDate`) sat unused — this wouldn't have compiled.

**What I did:**
1. Fixed the compile error by wiring the code to actually use the date-keyed tracking the doc comment described.
2. Verified build (Debug + Release) and full test suite (211/211) pass.
3. Dispatched `swift-reviewer` (sonnet) since this touches real logic. It found one real MEDIUM bug: the once-per-day flag was in-memory only, so it would silently refire the metric on every app relaunch after the buddy strip was already unlocked that day — corrupting the exact funnel metric this instrumentation exists to measure.
4. Fixed it properly: added a persisted, account-scoped `LocalDefaults` flag (`mutualRevealUnlockedLocalDate`/`mutualRevealUnlockedAccountID`), mirroring the repo's existing `milestoneAccountID` pattern, wired into `resetAccountScopedValues()`.
5. Re-verified: build + 211/211 tests green.
6. Checked off the TODO item in `.loop/VISION.md` with an honest note about the bug and fix, updated `.loop/state.json`, and committed with explicit paths (no `git add -A`, per repo guardrail).

**Not done / remaining:** 13 other unchecked TODO items remain (invite affordance, onFriendshipCreated trigger, share control, 50-source design research, Today/Buddies/Onboarding redesigns, N-way buddy UI, multi-alarm, motion-gated dismissal, ASO comparison, final full-suite/Release confirmation). `.loop/verify.sh` still correctly exits non-zero. The driver will pick up the next item on its next iteration.
